    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "607n8d3",
      "content": "Soil is the uppermost layer of the earth’s crust capable of supporting plant life. It develops through the long process of weathering of rocks combined with organic matter, relief, climate, organisms and time. India possesses a wide variety of soils due to its diverse geology, relief and climatic conditions. "
