    {
      "id": "fjsmkur",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Major Soil Types in India"
    },
    {
      "id": "aa2wi4m",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "ef9yhkp",
      "src": "/books/Precis/RRB COMPLETE GK/images/image_ef9yhkp.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "xomqtmk",
      "content": "Indian soils are broadly classified into six major types: Alluvial, Black, Red, Laterite, Desert (Arid), Forest/Mountain soils. Additionally, saline and peat soils occur locally.<img></img>"
    },
